course: dictionary
lesson: 9960
title: Colour words that paint a picture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tawny is a colour word. It means a warm orange-brown or yellowish-brown, like a lion's fur. Writers choose colour words to help you see a scene in your mind.
explain: «Then they chatter of violet seas, tawny sands, and lizard-haunted walls.» The sentence is about a place, so tawny sands must be a colour picture. Golden brown fits the sand, and the other colour words in the list help you see it too.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the word. «The twit-twoo of a British wood is usually two tawny owls.» Here tawny comes before owls, and it is part of the bird's name. A tawny owl is a common brown owl, so you know tawny is describing a kind of owl.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If brown fits where tawny is, and the picture still makes sense, you have found a good meaning.
fact: Tawny means a warm orange-brown or yellowish-brown colour.
fact: A tawny owl is a common brown owl found in Britain and Europe.
fact: «Tawny» is an adjective, so it can change to «tawnier» and «tawniest» to compare shades.
fact: Owls cannot move their eyes, so they turn their heads, up to about 270 degrees.
fact: Camouflage helps an animal look like the things around it, so a tawny owl looks like bark.
exercise: «Then they chatter of violet seas, tawny sands, and lizard-haunted walls.» What colour are the tawny sands? | Snowy white | Bright blue | *Golden brown | Deep green
exercise: A tawny owl is a common bird in Britain and Europe. What kind of bird is a tawny owl? | *A brown owl | A bird that cannot fly | A sea bird that swims | A yellow bird with a red beak
exercise: «A tawny owl looks like bark.» Why is the owl hard to see? | It is very large | *Its colour matches the bark | It sings all day | It is glowing
test: The text says «fulvous» and «tawny» are old words for what colour? | Sky blue | Pure white | *Golden yellow-brown | Bright red
test: Which word is the comparative form of tawny? | tawny-ish | tawniest | tawnily | *tawnier
exam: A story says «her hair was tawny in the sunlight». What does tawny tell the reader? | Her hair was missing | Her hair was blue | Her hair was wet | *Her hair was golden brown
